{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.longitude_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.longitude_row","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L81-L88","doc":"The longitude row at the cubic shape, `z₂⁵ z₃⁻¹ (1−z₀)⁴(1−z₁)⁴(1−z₂)⁻³(1−z₃)⁷` with\n`z₂ = z₃`, cleared: `(θ²−1)⁴ (1−θ)⁸ (2−θ²)⁴ = 1` — the fourth power of the meridian identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.meridian_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.meridian_row","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L76-L79","doc":"The meridian row at the cubic shape: `z₂ (1−z₀)(1−z₁)(1−z₃) = (θ²−1)(1−θ)²(2−θ²) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.all_rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.all_rows","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L61-L66","doc":"All four derived rows hold at the cubic shape, bundled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_two","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L54-L59","doc":"Row 2, `(0,0,−1,−1 | −2,−2,−1,−1 ; +)`: `1 / (z₂ z₃ (1−z₀)² (1−z₁)² (1−z₂)(1−z₃)) = 1`,\ncleared: `(θ²−1)² (1−θ)⁴ (2−θ²)² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_one","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L48-L52","doc":"Row 1, `(1,1,−1,−1 | 1,1,1,1 ; +)`: `z₀ z₁ (1−z₀)(1−z₁)(1−z₂)(1−z₃) / (z₂ z₃) = 1`, cleared:\n`θ² (1−θ)² (2−θ²)² = (θ²−1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_four","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L43-L46","doc":"Row 4 is row 3 with `z₁` in place of `z₀`; the shapes coincide, so it is the same identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.row_three","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L37-L41","doc":"Row 3, `(−1,0,1,1 | 1,0,0,0 ; −)`: `−(1 − z₀) z₂ z₃ / z₀ = 1`, cleared of the denominator, at\n`z₀ = θ`, `z₂ = z₃ = θ² − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.shape_cubic_discriminant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.shape_cubic_discriminant","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FiveTwoGluingFromFareyWord.lean#L34-L35","doc":"The shape field of `5₂`: the cubic `x³ − x + 1` has discriminant `−4·(−1)³ − 27·1² = −23`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}